agbcc_arm_patched: four opt-in options for the IWRAM ARM code
=============================================================

Applies to SAT-R/agbcc's gcc_arm (2.9-arm-000512) with `patch -p1` from
the agbcc checkout's root. tools/build_patched_agbcc_arm.sh does that on
a copy and installs the result as tools/agbcc/bin/agbcc_arm_patched.
tools/build_agbccpp.sh applies it, with the paths rewritten to g++_arm/,
to notyourav/agbcc's `cp` branch's ARM C++ compiler (the same
config/arm/arm.c and arm.h) and installs tools/agbcc/bin/agbcp_arm_patched,
the compiler the Makefile builds the IWRAM ARM code with.

Why: Crash Bandicoot XS's IWRAM ARM code was built by a later build of
agbcc_arm's own Cygnus/Red Hat ARM gcc line. That build isn't public.
Its code generation is agbcc_arm's, apart from two fixed strings in the
prologue/return code (docs/matching/iwram-image.md, fifth to seventh
passes) and two jump-pass rules it doesn't have (ninth step). These
options reproduce those four behaviours and nothing else:

  -mleaf-no-lr-save     A function that never uses or clobbers lr (no
                        calls, lr never allocated) and has no frame
                        pointer saves only its call-saved registers:
                        `stmfd sp!, {r4, r5, r6}' ... `ldmfd sp!, {r4,
                        r5, r6}; bx lr'. Stock agbcc_arm always adds lr
                        to the push (arm_expand_prologue, "If we have to
                        push any regs, then we must push lr as well") and
                        to the restore. Used by itoa_arm.

  -minterwork-return-lr An interworking return insn without a frame
                        pointer pops the return address into lr and
                        returns with `bx lr' (`ldmfd sp!, {lr}; bx lr').
                        Stock agbcc_arm pops into ip and returns with
                        `bx ip' (output_return_instruction). Used by
                        LookupSpriteFrameCache.

  -mno-cond-return      No conditional return insns: use_return_insn
                        (TRUE) is false, so jump.c leaves a conditional
                        branch to a label followed by the function's
                        return as a branch (`beq .L; ... .L: bx lr').
                        Stock agbcc_arm turns it into `bxeq lr' in any
                        frameless function with nothing saved. Used by
                        strncpy_arm.

  -mstrict-cross-jump   jump.c's find_cross_jump needs its full minimum
                        of matching insns when the run it finds starts
                        right after a label. Stock agbcc_arm lowers the
                        minimum by one there ("those jumps will be
                        tensioned"), so it merges two identical
                        `cmp; ble' loop tests that each follow a label.
                        Used by HeapSortActorsByKey.

All are off by default. With none given, every code path is the stock
one, so the compiler's output is byte-identical to agbcc_arm's.

Hunks:
  arm.h  1. ARM_FLAG_LEAF_NO_LR_SAVE / ARM_FLAG_INTERWORK_RETURN_LR bits
            (the next free target_flags bits after ARM_FLAG_LONG_CALLS),
            then ARM_FLAG_NO_COND_RETURN / ARM_FLAG_STRICT_CROSS_JUMP.
         2. TARGET_LEAF_NO_LR_SAVE / TARGET_INTERWORK_RETURN_LR /
            TARGET_NO_COND_RETURN / TARGET_STRICT_CROSS_JUMP.
         3. The -m[no-]leaf-no-lr-save / -m[no-]interwork-return-lr /
            -mno-cond-return (-mcond-return) / -m[no-]strict-cross-jump
            entries in TARGET_SWITCHES.
         4. INITIAL_ELIMINATION_OFFSET: no lr slot between the saved
            registers and the incoming stack arguments when lr isn't
            pushed, so argument offsets stay right.
         5. Prototype for arm_lr_save_skipped.
  arm.c  6. use_return_insn: no conditional return insn under
            -mno-cond-return; and no return insn when registers are saved
            but lr isn't (a return insn would pop the return address
            from lr's missing slot); the text epilogue handles it. With
            interworking this was already the case.
         7. output_return_instruction: under -minterwork-return-lr, pop
            into lr instead of ip ...
         8. ... and `bx lr' instead of `bx ip'.
         9. arm_lr_save_skipped: the one predicate for -mleaf-no-lr-save
            (option on, no frame pointer, lr never live).
        10. output_func_epilogue: leave lr out of the restore when the
            prologue left it out of the push.
        11. arm_expand_prologue: leave lr out of the push.
  jump.c 12. find_cross_jump: no lowered minimum after a label under
            -mstrict-cross-jump (inside #ifdef TARGET_STRICT_CROSS_JUMP,
            so the file stays target-independent).

g++_arm/'s jump.c differs from gcc_arm/'s elsewhere (coverage and
branch-probability code), so hunk 12 applies there at an offset.

